%N A001282 One-half of the number of permutations p of [n] having exactly three runs of adjacent entries differing by 1.
%C A001282 Old name: Number of permutations of length n by rises.
%D A001282 F. N. David, M. G. Kendall and D. E. Barton, Symmetric Function and Allied Tables, Cambridge, 1966, p. 264.
%D A001282 N. J. A. Sloane, A Handbook of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1973 (includes this sequence).
%D A001282 N. J. A. Sloane and Simon Plouffe, The Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1995 (includes this sequence).
%H A001282 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A001282/b001282.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 6..450</a>
%F A001282 G.f.: (1/(1-x)^9) * Sum_{k>=0} k! * ((1+x)^2*binomial(k+1,1)^2 - 8*(1+x)*binomial(k+2,2)^2 + 24*binomial(k+3,3)^2) * (x*(1-x)/(1+x))^(k+6). - _Seiichi Manyama_, Sep 01 2026
%o A001282 (PARI) my(N=20, x='x+O('x^N)); Vec(sum(k=0, N, k!*((1+x)^2*binomial(k+1,1)^2-8*(1+x)*binomial(k+2, 2)^2+24*binomial(k+3, 3)^2)*(x*(1-x)/(1+x))^(k+6))/(1-x)^9) \\ _Seiichi Manyama_, Sep 01 2026
